  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "<blockquote><p>Copper ores contain iron as the main impurity. Iron react with silica and is removed as slag. Therefore, the slag formed in the blast furnace is <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msub><mi>FeSiO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>.</p><p>The reaction that takes place in the blast furnace is as follows:</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>FeO</mi><mo>+</mo><msub><mi>SiO</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>&#8594;</mo><msub><mi>FeSiO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math>(slag)</p></blockquote>",
